int fib(int n, int[] memo) {
    if (n <= 0) return 0;
    else if (n == 1) return 1;
    else if (memo[n] > 0) return memo[n];

    memo[n] = fib(n - 1, memo) + fib(n - 2, memo);
    return memo[n];
} Explanation: Each Fibonacci number is calculated only once. Total calls: O(n).

